    "title": "Finding the Pivot Columns of a Matrix in Row Echelon Form"
  },
  "question": {
    ":question/problem": "The row echelon form matrix $M$ is given below. What are the pivot columns of $M?$\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -7 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $M$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $3$rd, and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & -7 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
